chapter_notes.1B:
Exposure assessment for Chapter 1B: `material_exposure`. Putin had direct presidential nuclear authority, crisis authority over mobilization/annexation signaling, and real leverage over treaty and safety posture in 2022. No score here.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"'No other option': Excerpts of Putin's speech declaring war","publisher":"Al Jazeera","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/2/24/putins-speech-declaring-war-on-ukraine-translated-excerpts","claim":"Putin framed the February 24 invasion as a necessary security move, warned that a direct attack on Russia would bring catastrophic consequences, and said Ukraine should not be allowed to acquire nuclear weapons.","locator":"lines 122-140, 157","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct transcript excerpt published the day of the invasion, translated from the Kremlin recording.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022-period primary speech evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Putin as the speaking president.","contrary_evidence":["The speech is self-justifying propaganda, not an independent account of the war's causes."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.5","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Factbox-What is the chain of command for potential Russian nuclear strikes?","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-03-02","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/factboxwhat-is-the-chain-of-command-for-potential-russian-nuclear-strikes-2776432","claim":"The Reuters factbox says the Russian president decides whether to use nuclear weapons, the Cheget briefcase transmits launch orders to the General Staff, and the 2020 doctrine lists scenarios including threats to the state's existence.","locator":"lines 410-435","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters factbox with a clear explanation of the command chain and doctrine, widely cited and contemporaneous.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly relevant to Putin's 2022 launch authority and command responsibility.","ruler_attribution":"Ruler-level authority is explicit: the president takes the decision to use nuclear weapons.","contrary_evidence":["This is institutional context, not proof of a specific launch order or safety reform."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Amidst Nuclear Saber Rattling, New START Treaty Demonstrates Importance","publisher":"Federation of American Scientists","publication_date":"2022-04-06","url":"https://fas.org/publication/new_start_treaty_importance/","claim":"After the invasion and Putin's high-alert order, FAS described the move as nuclear saber rattling; it also noted that New START data exchanges continued and that Russia still had a large, modernizing strategic force.","locator":"lines 46-51, 57, 73-90","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Technical arms-control analysis grounded in State Department data and contemporaneous reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 force posture and arms-control behavior.","ruler_attribution":"Relates directly to Putin's post-invasion nuclear signaling and the Russian force posture he oversaw.","contrary_evidence":["The piece also notes that New START limits and exchanges still continued, which is a restraint signal."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.4","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia Further Pauses New START Inspections","publisher":"Arms Control Association","publication_date":"2022-09","url":"https://www.armscontrol.org/act/2022-09/news/russia-further-pauses-new-start-inspections","claim":"Russia told the United States in August 2022 that it would prohibit on-site New START inspections, which reduced verification and delayed a return to treaty transparency.","locator":"lines 80-87","source_type":"ngo","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed arms-control reporting with treaty context and direct quotation of the Russian justification.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly the 2022 period in question.","ruler_attribution":"The move occurred under Putin's presidency and shaped Russia's treaty posture.","contrary_evidence":["Russia said the move was caused by sanctions and inspection logistics, not by treaty rejection."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin's speech: Read the address on Russia's partial military mobilization","publisher":"The Washington Post","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2022/09/21/putin-speech-russia-ukraine-war-mobilization/","claim":"In the September 21 address, Putin said Russia faced nuclear blackmail, tied that claim to Zaporizhzhia safety fears, and warned that use of all available weapons was not bluffing if territorial integrity was threatened.","locator":"lines 80-83","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"The Post published the Kremlin translation of the speech in full and flagged the nuclear passages directly.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 crisis speech during wartime escalation.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Putin as the speaker and decision-maker.","contrary_evidence":["Putin later denied that Russia had openly threatened nuclear use."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.5","1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin drafts up to 300,000 reservists, backs annexation amid war losses","publisher":"The Washington Post","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2022/09/21/putin-speech-annexation-ukraine-russia/","claim":"Reuters' transcript-based coverage says Putin backed annexation moves, ordered partial mobilization, and hinted that he was ready to use nuclear weapons to defend Russian territory as he defined it.","locator":"lines 36-36","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Secondary but contemporaneous transcript-based reporting that independently corroborates the nuclear threat framing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Same-day coverage of the key September 21 turning point.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Putin's public wartime decision-making.","contrary_evidence":["This is corroborative reporting, not the original transcript."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.5","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Reaction to Russia mobilising more troops for Ukraine","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://uk.investing.com/news/world-news/reaction-to-russias-vladimir-putin-mobilising-more-troops-for-ukraine-2757122","claim":"Reuters reported that Putin made a thinly veiled nuclear threat while announcing mobilization, and that NATO leaders described the move as reckless and desperate.","locator":"search result snippet and Reuters report title/summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Useful contemporaneous corroboration, but the accessible page was only partially retrievable in this session.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Immediate reaction to the September 21 escalation.","ruler_attribution":"Centers Putin's public nuclear signaling after battlefield setbacks.","contrary_evidence":["Because only partial access was available, I am using it as corroborative context rather than a standalone anchor."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.5"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Kremlin scolds West for 'provocative' nuclear rhetoric","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-10-12","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/commodities-news/kremlin-scolds-west-for-provocative-nuclear-rhetoric-2910292","claim":"Reuters reported that the Kremlin repeated Putin's Sept. 21 warning that he was not bluffing and said Western nuclear rhetoric was provocative, showing how the leadership normalized escalation language rather than de-escalating it.","locator":"lines 406-412","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Clear Reuters reporting with direct attribution to the Kremlin spokesman and the September 21 warning.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"October 2022 follow-up to the September nuclear threat.","ruler_attribution":"This is directly tied to Putin's warning and the Kremlin's defense of it.","contrary_evidence":["The Kremlin presented the posture as defensive deterrence rather than escalation."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin asserts control over Ukraine nuclear plant, Kyiv disagrees","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-10-05","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/putin-asserts-control-over-ukraine-nuclear-plant-kyiv-disagrees-2905308","claim":"Putin ordered his government to take control of Zaporizhzhia while IAEA warned the plant's power supply was extremely fragile and the site had become a focus of nuclear-disaster concern.","locator":"lines 403-407","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong contemporaneous reporting tying Putin's order to a live nuclear-safety risk.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 wartime nuclear-safety crisis.","ruler_attribution":"The order is attributable to Putin and his wartime control over occupied territory.","contrary_evidence":["Russia said it was securing the plant, while Ukraine said the move was an illegal land grab."],"lenses":["1B.5","1B.9","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia Blocks NPT Conference Consensus Over Ukraine","publisher":"Arms Control Association","publication_date":"2022-09","url":"https://www.armscontrol.org/act/2022-09/news/russia-blocks-npt-conference-consensus-over-ukraine","claim":"Russia blocked the 2022 NPT Review Conference from consensus over wording on the Zaporizhzhia nuclear safety crisis, linking Putin's wartime occupation policy to a breakdown in multilateral nonproliferation diplomacy.","locator":"lines 73-80","source_type":"ngo","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Explicit, date-specific arms-control reporting with a clear causal link between Russian conduct and treaty failure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly matches the 2022 review conference period.","ruler_attribution":"The obstruction occurred under Putin's presidency and reflected his war policy.","contrary_evidence":["Russia said the conference text was politicized and anti-Russian."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.5","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"States Prepare for Nonproliferation Conference","publisher":"Arms Control Association","publication_date":"2022-07","url":"https://www.armscontrol.org/act/2022-07/news/states-prepare-nonproliferation-conference","claim":"The Feb. 24 invasion of Ukraine, after Ukraine had given up nuclear weapons in return for security assurances, raised serious doubts about Russia's intentions as a nuclear-weapon state.","locator":"lines 83-83","source_type":"ngo","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Directly connects the invasion to damaged confidence in Russia's nuclear responsibility and nonproliferation credibility.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Sets the 2022 diplomatic baseline for arms-control and nonproliferation judgments.","ruler_attribution":"The invasion was ordered by Putin and drove the doubt about Russia's intentions.","contrary_evidence":["This is a diplomatic critique, not a technical assessment of the arsenal itself."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.5","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"7. World nuclear forces","publisher":"SIPRI","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.sipri.org/yearbook/2023/07","claim":"SIPRI says Russia and the United States continued large modernization and replacement programs for their nuclear forces, and that global operational warheads were no longer falling cleanly.","locator":"lines 88-90","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"High-quality technical yearbook material, though this page is a 2023 overview rather than a 2022 event log.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Post-2022 retrospective context on the posture Putin inherited and intensified.","ruler_attribution":"Context for the posture Putin controlled in 2022, not a discrete Putin decision on its own.","contrary_evidence":["This does not prove a 2022 ruler-level decision by itself."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin insists U.S. respect 'multipolar' world and tell Kyiv to seek peace","publisher":"The Washington Post","publication_date":"2022-10-27","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2022/10/27/vladimir-putin-speech-valdai-war/","claim":"Putin said Russia had not openly threatened to use nuclear weapons and had no need to do so in Ukraine, while also repeating false dirty-bomb claims.","locator":"lines 60-62","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting of Putin's own denial, useful as contrary evidence against the Sept. 21 threat posture.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late-2022 retrospective statement on the same conflict.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Putin.","contrary_evidence":["The denial sits alongside the earlier Sept. 21 threat and does not erase it."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.5","1B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"No change to U.S. nuclear posture due to Russia threats, Pentagon says","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-27","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/general/no-change-to-us-nuclear-posture-due-to-russia-threats-pentagon-says-2900188","claim":"Reuters reported that U.S. officials still saw no immediate change to American nuclear posture, even while saying Russia's threats were serious and a Russian ally outlined a nuclear strike scenario on Ukraine.","locator":"lines 427-431","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Useful independent corroboration of the threat environment, though it reports U.S. reactions rather than Putin's decision directly.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Immediate aftermath of the September nuclear threat.","ruler_attribution":"Indirectly tied to Putin's threat environment and its strategic effects.","contrary_evidence":["The article describes U.S. posture, not a Russian action beyond the threatening environment."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Analysis-Truth or bluff? Why Putin's nuclear warnings have the West worried","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-28","url":"https://m.investing.com/news/world-news/analysistruth-or-bluff-why-putins-nuclear-warnings-have-the-west-worried-2900363?ampMode=1","claim":"Reuters said Putin's warning to defend Russia with nuclear weapons after annexation moves made Western concern about escalation more urgent and prompted debate over whether Moscow was bluffing.","locator":"lines 10-12, 51-53","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Analytical Reuters piece summarizing the strategic meaning of the warning and the expert debate it triggered.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly about the late-September 2022 crisis point.","ruler_attribution":"Centers Putin's own warning and the annexation-linked escalation pathway.","contrary_evidence":["Analysis pieces are interpretive and do not prove intent to use nuclear weapons."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.5","1B.8","1B.10"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidates found: about 48
- Documents opened or partially opened: 31
- Duplicate families removed: about 16
- Irrelevant / out-of-period / weak context-only items dropped: about 7
- Inaccessible or timeout-blocked documents: about 10
- Accepted distinct URLs this wave: 13
- Domains searched: 11
- Domains retained in accepted evidence this wave: 6

Material gaps:
- I still do not have clean, openable official Kremlin/Pravo pages for the 2020 nuclear deterrence doctrine text or the 2022 decrees, so those remain discovery-only for now.
- IAEA 2022 Zaporizhzhia updates were visible in search but several direct opens timed out; they are the next best target for Chapter 1B.5/1B.9.
- I do not yet have strong public evidence on 1B.7 style issues: internal expert appointments, loyalty filtering, or whether Putin added risk-reducing specialists versus loyalists around the nuclear/security apparatus.
- A U.S. State Department 2022 New START compliance report would be useful for tightening the treaty/inspection sub-claim.

Compact event map:
- Feb 24: invasion speech, security framing, and nuclearized deterrence language.
- Feb 27-Mar: nuclear high-alert signaling and emergency war posture.
- Aug: New START inspection pause becomes a clear transparency setback.
- Sep 21: mobilization plus explicit nuclear threat and ZNPP nuclear-blackmail framing.
- Sep 30-Oct 5: annexation push and Zaporizhzhia control order intensify existential-risk exposure.
- Oct 12-27: Kremlin defends nuclear rhetoric; Putin later downplays that he threatened nuclear use.
- Late 2022: Russia blocks NPT consensus over Zaporizhzhia safety wording.

Chapter source plan:
- Keep as anchors: the Feb. 24 transcript, the Sept. 21 mobilization speech, the Reuters chain-of-command factbox, the New START inspection story, the Zaporizhzhia control story, and the NPT blockade story.
- Keep as corroboration/contrary balance: Reuters reaction coverage, the Valdai denial, the Pentagon posture story, and the Reuters analysis on bluff versus real threat.
- Add next wave if needed: official Kremlin/Pravo doctrine and decrees, IAEA 2022 ZNPP updates, and the U.S. State Department New START compliance report.

