- The Chechnya record would benefit from a 2022 or late-2022 source from an official inquiry, UN mechanism, or a tightly dated investigative report on kidnappings and disappearances.
- I have strong evidence for protest repression, censorship, torture, LGBT discrimination, and domestic-violence neglect, but less on positive restraint or effective remedy, which itself is an important signal for this chapter.
- If you want a second discovery wave, the next best queries are: 2022 Russian court records on anti-war "fake news" cases, 2022 regional domestic-violence reports, and 2022 prison-oversight or ombudsman material.

