SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin tells Russian business people he had no choice over Ukraine","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/putin-tells-russian-business-people-he-had-no-choice-over-ukraine-2771505","claim":"Putin told Russian business leaders that he had no choice but to order the operation against Ukraine and framed the war as a forced decision.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is a high-quality wire service; the claim reports Putin's own remarks contemporaneously.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"direct speech by Putin, fully attributable to him","contrary_evidence":["Later reporting showed the invasion was a deliberate strategic choice, not an unavoidable necessity."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.3","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine urges halt to Russia's assault as Biden heads to Poland","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-03-25","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/ukraine-urges-halt-to-russias-assault-as-biden-heads-to-poland-2791645","claim":"Reuters reported that Moscow was scaling back its ambitions after setbacks near Kyiv and shifting focus to the eastern Donbass region.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is a strong contemporaneous news source and the article reports observable battlefield/strategy changes.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Putin ultimately controlled the war strategy, though the shift also reflected military setbacks and subordinate implementation.","contrary_evidence":["The article also reflects pressure from battlefield failure rather than voluntary strategic refinement."],"lenses":["8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Kommersant reports Russia will reduce military activity on Kyiv and Chernihiv fronts after Istanbul talks","publisher":"Kommersant","publication_date":"2022-03-29","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/5282398","claim":"Russia said it would reduce military activity on the Kyiv and Chernihiv fronts after the Istanbul talks and had received Ukrainian written proposals on neutrality.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Domestic reporting is useful for the statement and chronology, though it is less independent than international wire reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Putin's government controlled the negotiation posture and military response, but the move was also shaped by battlefield conditions.","contrary_evidence":["Whether this was a genuine de-escalation or a tactical redeployment remained disputed."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin orders new budget rules to boost Russia's growth","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-06-09","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/putin-orders-new-budget-rules-to-boost-russias-growth-2834324","claim":"Putin ordered new budget rules and said they should ensure stability of public finances and raise growth rates.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reports a concrete policy directive from Putin tied to fiscal management and growth goals.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"directly attributable to Putin as head of state ordering the policy change","contrary_evidence":["The article does not itself prove effective implementation, only intent and formal direction."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's Putin proposes to reappoint central bank chief Nabiullina","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-03-18","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/russias-putin-proposes-to-reappoint-central-bank-chief-nabiullina-2787264","claim":"Putin proposed reappointing Elvira Nabiullina and Reuters reported that the move was framed as helping preserve macroeconomic stability.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is a strong source for the appointment and the public rationale attached to it.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"direct appointment power by Putin over a key economic official","contrary_evidence":["The central bank retained some operational autonomy, so competence credit is only partial and mediated."],"lenses":["8B.4","8B.5","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia increases its emergency spending fund by $46b","publisher":"The Straits Times / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-03-03","url":"https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/russia-increases-its-emergency-spending-fund-by-46b","claim":"Russia increased its emergency spending fund to support economic stability under sanctions and had already pledged more than 1 trillion roubles in anti-crisis support to businesses.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting, republished by a major outlet, describes a concrete fiscal response to sanctions shock.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Putin's government controlled the fiscal response, though execution also depended on ministries and the budget system.","contrary_evidence":["The move reflects crisis defense under duress rather than a clean growth expansion."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia economy: pensions","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-01-12","url":"https://www.euronews.com/next/2022/01/12/russia-economy-pensions","claim":"Putin called for an 8.6% pension increase above inflation and had previously ordered one-off social payments and public-sector salary hikes worth at least 500 billion roubles.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting captures a specific budget and distribution choice attributed to Putin.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"directly attributable to Putin's policy choice and public instruction","contrary_evidence":["The measure may have been partly compensatory because inflation was already running above plan."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin orders benefit payments for people arriving in Russia from Ukraine","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-11","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/putin-orders-benefit-payments-for-people-arriving-in-russia-from-ukraine-2881261","claim":"Putin signed a decree creating monthly pension payments and other benefits for people forced to leave Ukrainian territory for Russia.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reports a signed decree and the benefit structure, which are directly observable policy actions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"directly attributable to Putin's decree authority, though implementation ran through state agencies.","contrary_evidence":["This is a targeted wartime benefit and does not show broad welfare improvement."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia economy: Putin forum","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-08","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/08/russia-economy-putin-forum","claim":"Putin said Russia would post a budget surplus in 2022, forecast GDP would fall around 2 percent, and acknowledged that economic hardships remained for many Russians.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting captures Putin's public macroeconomic claims and expectations in September 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"direct public positioning by Putin, though the actual macro path depended on the central bank, finance ministry, war, and sanctions.","contrary_evidence":["Later data showed a more mixed picture than the optimistic framing suggested."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russian unemployment rate hits record low, economic data paints mixed picture","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-02","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/russian-unemployment-rate-hits-record-low-economic-data-paints-mixed-picture-2901110","claim":"Russia's unemployment fell to a record low of 3.8 percent, but real wages fell 3.2 percent year on year in July and car production dropped 69 percent.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is a strong source for contemporaneous economic outcomes reported from official data.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"outcomes were only partly attributable to Putin because they also reflected sanctions, war disruption, and central bank actions.","contrary_evidence":["Low unemployment coexisted with falling wages and severe sectoral contraction."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's 2022 economic fall seen in lower incomes, slumping consumer demand","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-12-28","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/russias-2022-economic-fall-seen-in-lower-incomes-slumping-consumer-demand-2998520","claim":"Reuters reported Rosstat data showing real disposable incomes fell 1 percent in 2022, retail sales slumped 6.7 percent, and consumer demand contracted sharply.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is strong for reporting official statistical releases and the article gives specific year-end outcomes.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"mixed attribution: Putin's war and sanctions policy mattered, but so did external sanctions and household behavior.","contrary_evidence":["The same article noted some labor-market resilience, so the downturn was uneven rather than absolute."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia says budget deficit hit 2.3% of GDP in 2022","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2023-01-10","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/russia-says-budget-deficit-hit-23-of-gdp-in-2022-2977210","claim":"Reuters reported that Russia recorded a 2022 budget deficit of 2.3 percent of GDP and had to draw on its rainy-day fund while diverting more money toward security and defense.","locator":"article text","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is a strong source for the fiscal outcome and the allocation tradeoff." ,"final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"retrospective evidence about the 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"Putin's war and spending priorities were central, but the fiscal outcome also reflected sanctions and energy prices.","contrary_evidence":["The deficit was manageable by sovereign standards, so this is a mixed rather than catastrophic signal."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bank of Russia raises key rate because inflation was above forecast","publisher":"Bank of Russia","publication_date":"2022-02-11","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/eng/press/pr?file=11022022_133000Key_eng.htm","claim":"The central bank raised the key rate because inflation was above forecast and demand was outpacing output capacity.","locator":"press release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary official monetary-policy statement with explicit rationale and date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"indirect: the Bank of Russia acted under its own mandate, though the broader policy environment was shaped by Putin's state","contrary_evidence":["This reflects central-bank autonomy, so it cannot be credited fully to Putin alone."],"lenses":["8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.8","8B.9"]}
